📦 What is Java Collections Framework?
Java Collections are data structures used to store, manipulate, and retrieve groups of objects efficiently.

It includes interfaces and classes for:

Lists

Sets

Maps

Queues

Stacks

And more...

All classes are part of java.util package.

🧩 Core Interfaces in Collections
| Interface | Description                           | Common Implementations                             |
| --------- | ------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |
| **List**  | Ordered collection, allows duplicates | `ArrayList`, `LinkedList`, `Vector`                |
| **Set**   | No duplicates allowed                 | `HashSet`, `LinkedHashSet`, `TreeSet`              |
| **Queue** | Follows FIFO, ordered processing      | `PriorityQueue`, `ArrayDeque`                      |
| **Map**   | Key-value pairs, no duplicate keys    | `HashMap`, `LinkedHashMap`, `TreeMap`, `Hashtable` |


📘 Common Classes and Usage
✅ List
